From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chelovechishee <261262090+chelovechishee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 49/53] media: i2c: add the Samsung S5K4HA and S5K5E9 sensors

The rear (S5K4HA, 8 MP, 4 lanes) and front (S5K5E9, 5 MP, 2 lanes)
cameras of the Galaxy Tab A 10.1 (2019), modelled on the s5k3m5 driver:
a full size and a 2x2 binned RAW10 mode each, exposure, analogue gain
(read from the sensor's own limits), blanking, flips and test patterns.
The register settings come from the downstream fimc-is set files B.

The S5K4HA keeps its focus lens (the lens-focus device) powered with it:
the lens's I2C bus only works while the sensor's I/O rail is up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig  |  14 +
 drivers/media/i2c/Makefile |   2 +
 drivers/media/i2c/s5k4ha.c | 946 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/media/i2c/s5k5e9.c | 892 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 1854 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/i2c/s5k4ha.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/i2c/s5k5e9.c

